--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. DEFINITIONS & SCOPE OF PROTECTED ASSETS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
This repository and all associated documentation, files, diagrams, specifications, 
and configurations (collectively referred to as "Technical Materials") comprise 
proprietary operational and technical guidelines designed specifically for the 
execution of Ibadah Perdana UKK UNNES 2026.

Protected Technical Materials include, but are not limited to:
a. Broadcast, Camera Acquisition, and Wireless Video Transmission System Schematics.
b. Master Signal Flow, Video Switching, HDMI Splitter, and Multi-Screen LED Mapping Protocols.
c. Audio Sub-Mixing, Digital Routing (Yamaha QL5 & NewBaxs CT80S), and FOH Remote Architecture.
d. Stage Time Keeper and Independent Stage Monitoring Workflows.
e. Electrical and Power Distribution Safety and Ground-Loop Prevention Topologies.
f. Master Inventory, Equipment Tracking, Ownership Attribution, and Storage Allocations.
g. Rundown Sequences, Media Asset Target Displays, and Operator Responsibility Matrices.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. GRANT OF INTERNAL ACCESS & AUTHORIZED USE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Access to and use of these Technical Materials is strictly limited to authorized 
members of:
a. Panitia Ibadah Perdana UKK UNNES 2026 (Organizing Committee).
b. System Engineers, Media Engineers, and Creative Engineers.
c. Assigned Camera Operators, Audio Technicians, Visual/Lyrics Operators, and Stage Crews.
d. Authorized volunteers and technical servants acting under the direct supervision 
   of the Production Lead / System Engineer.

Authorized personnel are granted a non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable right 
to consult, review, and execute these materials solely for the preparation, rehearsal, 
live production, and post-event decommissioning of Ibadah Perdana UKK UNNES 2026.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. RESTRICTIONS & PROHIBITED ACTIONS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Except as expressly authorized in writing by the System Engineer or Production Lead, 
any party possessing or accessing this repository is strictly prohibited from:
a. Copying, publishing, distributing, licensing, sublicensing, or transmitting 
   these Technical Materials to external parties or unauthorized public forums.
b. Making public mirrors, forks, or derivative works without explicit written 
   consent from the technical leadership.
c. Utilizing these proprietary system schematics, wiring plans, or operational 
   blueprints for non-affiliated commercial productions or unauthorized third-party events.
d. Altering equipment attribution records, inventory tracking labels, or safety 
   guidelines without proper technical review and authorization.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. EQUIPMENT RESPONSIBILITY, SAFETY & INTEGRITY
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
a. All hardware, cameras, lenses, converters, splitters, mixers, transmitters, and 
   laptops listed within the inventory records are loaned in good faith from 
   respective vendors, churches (GIA Deliksari, GKJ Ngaliyan), campus organizations 
   (UKK UNNES), venue facilities (Auditorium UNNES), and personal contributors.
b. Handlers, operators, and technical crews are required to exercise the highest 
   standards of operational care, electrical safety protocols, and physical security 
   during setup, live operation, and teardown ("usung-usung").
c. Any equipment anomaly, signal degradation, physical defect, or missing item must 
   be immediately reported to the System Engineer (Andreas) and Media Lead (Richard).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
5. MODIFICATIONS, GOVERNANCE & AMENDMENTS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The Production Lead / System Engineer reserves the full authority to modify, 
expand, amend, or revoke technical pipelines, routing topologies, operator 
allocations, and inventory statuses at any time prior to or during the event to 
ensure operational excellence and maximum system stability.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
6. DISCLAIMER OF EXTERNAL WARRANTY
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
THESE TECHNICAL MATERIALS ARE PROVIDED "AS IS" EXCLUSIVELY FOR INTERNAL EVENT 
EXECUTION. THE PRODUCTION TEAM MAKES NO WARRANTIES REGARDING APPLICABILITY FOR 
EXTERNAL PRODUCTION ENVIRONMENTS OUTSIDE THE SPECIFIC CONTEXT OF AUDITORIUM UNNES 
AND IBADAH PERDANA UKK UNNES 2026.
